# Don't track the cloned target repo or generated data
data/          # ignore anything inside a folder called "data" (where we'll save commit history JSON, and where the cloned repo will temporarily live)
__pycache__/   # ignore Python's auto-generated bytecode cache folders
*.pyc          # ignore individual compiled Python files (the * means "match anything ending in .pyc")
# since this project about to cloning the entire httpx repository (thousands of files) onto this computer so we can read its history.
# but do not want that huge external repo accidentally becoming part of my GitHub repo — that would be like accidentally committing someone else's entire library into my own project.